lesson: 231
title: Players in a team
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: Every sport has its own number of players in a team, and you are expected to know it: a soccer team and a cricket team each put 11 players out, a basketball team 5.
explain: To count the players of several teams, multiply the number of teams by the players in one team, sport by sport, and add.
explain: 2 soccer teams and 3 basketball teams with no substitutes: 2 × 11 = 22 and 3 × 5 = 15, so 22 + 15 = 37 players.
vars: a=name n=2..6 m=2..6
answer: n * 11 + m * 5
exercise: At a sports day there are {n} soccer teams and {m} basketball teams. Every team has just its players on the field, no substitutes. How many players are there in all?
exercise: A school has {n} soccer teams and {m} basketball teams, each with only its starting players. How many players are in these teams altogether?
exercise: {a} counts all the players: {n} cricket teams and {m} basketball teams are playing, with no substitutes. How many players does {a.he} count?
exercise: How many players take part if {n} soccer teams and {m} basketball teams each put a full team out, with nobody on the bench?
exercise: The club has {n} soccer teams and {m} basketball teams, and today every team plays with just its starting players. How many players are playing today?
exercise: In a tournament, {n} soccer teams and {m} basketball teams turn up with no reserves. How many players turn up?
exercise: {n} soccer teams n {m} basketball teams at the tournament, no subs. how many players altogether
exercise: ok so {n+1} — no wait {n} footy teams, soccer i mean, plus {m} basketball teams. no subs. how many players is that
exercise: {m} basketball teams and {n} soccer teams turning up, oh and the netball girls are on another day so don't count them. how many players, no reserves
exercise: my mate reckons {n*10+m*5} players for {n} soccer teams and {m} basketball teams lol. starters only, what's the real number
exercise: cricket {n} teams, basketball {m}, just the players who start. how many in total
test: With no one on the bench, what is the total number of players in {m} basketball teams and {n} soccer teams?
test: A coach drives to a tournament with {n} soccer sides and {m} basketball sides, each with exactly enough players to start. How many players come along?
test: Every starting player gets a new shirt: there are {n} soccer teams and {m} basketball teams. How many shirts are needed?
test: how many shirts for {n} soccer teams + {m} basketball teams, starters only
test: {a} makes one lunch for each player of {m} basketball teams and {n} cricket teams, no reserves. How many lunches does {a.he} make?
test: {n} soccer teams, {m} basketball, oh and {a} is the ref but not a player. how many players (no subs)
test: Only the starting players are counted. Together, how many players do {m} basketball teams and {n} cricket teams have?
exam: Determine the aggregate number of players comprised in {n.words} association football teams and {m.words} basketball teams, it being given that no team fields substitutes.
exam: It is given that {n} soccer teams and {m} basketball teams are each represented solely by their starting players. Ascertain the total number of participants.
exam: Pursuant to the regulations of the tournament, each of {n} cricket teams and {m} basketball teams fields only its starting players. Compute the total number of players fielded.
exam: Whereas {m} basketball teams and {n} soccer teams are in attendance, none of them with reserves, state the total number of players present.
exercise: After the club's "restructuring", only {n} soccer teams and {m} basketball teams are left, and none of them has substitutes. How many players are there?
exercise: {n} footy teams n {m} basketball teams turned up, the subs all had a "family emergency", aka hungover lol, so no subs. how many players, use ur head
test: The club calls its weakest teams "developing". On Saturday {n} soccer teams and {m} basketball teams play, the developing ones included, with no substitutes. How many players take part?
